    Derive the group row bits from the actual member layout
    
    The trusted planner now derives a group's row bits from the actual oracle
    members that join it: each member takes an aligned power-of-two block of main
    rows and of mask rows, the group's mask bits are the ceiling of the mask row
    sum, and its main bits are the maximum of the main row bits, the mask bits and
    one. Unit tests cover a request-sized group, unaligned member blocks, the
    table-sized shape, a mask-only group and the invalid member lists.
    
    This is the first piece of the sizing derivation; the code capacities, the
    random tails, the stage lists and the full round budget remain the next steps.

